## Preserved failures and follow-up repairs

The original public `CONFIRMATION_TARGET` failures remain failures. The **4-second window and 16 pressure workers** are unchanged; source-map reconciliation does not establish that this runtime deadline has been met.

The full local run on `dc42ce4d` stopped at the stale lifetime source lock; the later full run on `7d8d4c59` stopped at the hash-use source map. Both original outcomes and raw streams are retained. Subsequent metadata-only binding repairs are manually reviewed against their declared source inputs; their local controls are not relabelled as successful full-lane or hosted runs.

**Historical collector disposition:** {historical_collector_disposition}

That separate collector issue is not deemed repaired by the source-map changes above. Its retained historical results must not be rewritten as observations of the final candidate.

## Original system acceptance conditions remain

**Prior system qualification remains `HOLD_NO_GO / DENY_ALL`.** The retained original `0746` campaigns remain **0/3 passing and 0/9 phases passing**. History preservation, source checks, component tests and PR readiness do not waive the original system conditions.

The original **4-second Host service**, independent **30-second campaign**, and separate **History/capacity/churn** criteria require exact-source hosted evidence under their original contracts. The storage campaign still requires **at least three independently administered failure domains and at least 72 hours**. Failed or missing lanes remain open until their complete outcomes are collected.

Ordinary Hepta daemon stage-owner assembly and the **same-operation training/evaluation/Selection-or-NoUpdate/install/FinalUse/next-task/cold-recovery trace** remain subject to the original identity, ownership and recovery requirements. Test ELFs do not supply the ordinary-daemon binary, model, loader or evaluator identities.

Large-model BT with complete custody, independent WAN operators and failure domains, real payments and sustained leases, and the required long-run deployments retain their original contracts. The PoN cost/consensus and PQ proof obligations remain conditional or unresolved. **No acceptance deadline, threshold or denominator is waived, and no production activation is granted.**

## History retention and remaining repository actions

Recorded history tag: `{archive_tag}`  
Annotated tag object: `{tag_oid}`  
[Archive commit and exact manifests]({url}/tree/{archive_commit}): `{archive_commit}`  
Candidate explicitly captured by that archive: `{archive_candidate_head}`

The verified archive scope must retain all **892 original tips**, their reachable history and the exact 908-name manifest. The archive's captured candidate is stated separately from the final PR head; an older archive is not presented as containing later source or execution results. History retention does not assert semantic equivalence between alternatives or that every archived tip becomes an ancestor of linear main.

Main integration must use the protected linear merge route after the required exact-head and prospective-merge acceptance checks. Branch cleanup follows a verified merge and a fresh complete reference inventory. The observed protection on `fix/chain-bulk-state-tree-20261017` disallows deletion; that remains a distinct blocker to a one-branch result, and this update does not change protection.

The audit report also retains the unresolved macOS physical-retention observation and the 27 historical dependency registry/yank-query timeouts. Main integration and final branch cleanup are not completed by this PR metadata update.
